  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Biblical trauma healing in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the intervention is to expand Bible-based trauma healing in Ukraine by equipping facilitators with advanced skills and supporting vulnerable groups affected by war.

Participants include seven leading facilitators selected from over 80 candidates, and widows and orphans of fallen soldiers as well as families of active-duty soldiers.

Main activities include providing the facilitators with an 18-month modular master&#x2019;s program in psychology, organizing trauma healing camps, and running small-group programs at Trauma Healing Institute Restoration Centers in Kyiv and Lviv. 

The expected outcome is a stronger network of qualified facilitators and increased resilience among traumatized participants through healing programs and continued support.</narrative>
  </description>
